# Normalise line endings in the repository, not just in the working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf was true on the machine that created this repo, so files were
# committed as LF but checked out as CRLF on Windows. Prettier is configured with
# endOfLine: "lf", so `prettier --check` failed on 19 files that had never been
# edited - the drift was in the working tree, not in the content.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` lets git detect text vs binary itself, and pins the working
# tree to LF on every platform so a Windows contributor and a Linux CI run see the
# same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated or vendored assets that must stay byte-exact.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
